# test/mutations.list — F6 named-mutation registry (tier-2 surface)
#
# One mutation per line. A mutation "targets" a check when a seeded
# container run against the mutated tree no longer produces that
# check's expected finding, i.e. its check_id flips out of the audit
# output (or the seeded tier-2 driver fails on a probe for it).
#
# FORMAT — three tab-separated fields per entry line:
#
#   check_id <TAB> target <TAB> sed_expression
#
#   check_id        The check_id whose expected finding should flip
#                   out of the --json findings[] after the mutation.
#   target          Repo-relative path of the file the sed applies to
#                   (the driver applies it to a scratch copy of the
#                   tree and restores with git after each entry).
#   sed_expression  A single sed s-command, e.g.
#                   s|json_push alert security.fail2ban_banned security |json_push alert security.fail2ban_bannedX security |
#
# CONVENTIONS
#   - Lines beginning with '#' and blank lines are ignored.
#   - The sed uses '|' as the delimiter so the regex slashes (e.g.
#     /usr/bin/find) stay literal; no expression here needs '/'.
#   - Fields are applied verbatim by the driver with no shell
#     expansion: sed -i "<sed_expression>" "<target>".
#   - Dots in search strings are plain-text identifiers and match
#     'any char' in regex; that is harmless here because every
#     search string occurs on exactly one line of its target file
#     (verified at registry creation — keep it that way when adding
#     entries).
#   - Each entry must be a single line: no tabs, no backslash
#     line-continuations inside a field.
#   - Family A entries mutate the seeded STATE (seed.sh); family B
#     entries mutate the audit's own emission (scripts/box-audit.sh)
#     by renaming the check_id it pushes. Both families flip the
#     targeted check_id out of the output; family B is the only
#     family available for checks whose seed state is produced
#     post-boot by test/install-seeded.sh (sockets, bans, journal
#     lines) — those lines live in the driver, which the registry
#     must not edit.
#
# COVERAGE — one entry per check_id test/install-seeded.sh asserts,
# to the full seeded surface (fourteen total). install-seeded.sh
# asserts nine findings in test/install-seeded/assert-json.py
# (EXPECTED) plus four more inline (the F4 v6 block, the issue-#53
# v4 block, and the #38 delta-mode suid/security mutated-count
# probes); the registry carries those nine + four, i.e. every
# distinct check_id the seeded driver asserts:
#   security.fail2ban_banned, security.fail2ban_jail, security.new_port,
#   security.ssh_fails, security.outbound_remote_count,
#   security.outbound_remote_count_v6, security.suid_delta,
#   updates.security_pending, updates.security_delta,
#   system.failed_units, system.cron_d_dropins, system.user_cron,
#   maintenance.apt_cache_stale, integrity.change
#
# TERMINAL STATE PER ENTRY — FLIPPED or an explicit cannot-flip note.
# The driver's pristine baseline runs the SAME post-boot seed as
# install-seeded.sh EXCEPT the four findings that need (a) ESTAB
# sockets on lo (the F4/issue-#53 v4+v6 blocks run them AFTER the
# first audit) or (b) a mutated "yesterday" counts sidecar (the #38
# delta probes plant it AFTER the first audit). Those four are
# therefore ABSENT from the driver's baseline, and a mutation can
# only flip a check the baseline produced — so for them the
# terminal state is an explicit cannot-flip note (below), not a
# flip. This is the driver's documented "(absent-in-baseline)"
# signal, not a silent SURVIVED:
#
#   CHECKS THAT CANNOT BE FLIPPED BY A SINGLE SED (absent-in-baseline):
#   - security.outbound_remote_count (family B sed present; flips
#     only when the driver seeds ESTAB v4 sockets post-boot — it
#     does not; install-seeded.sh's issue-#53 block does, after the
#     first audit). cannot-flip.
#   - security.outbound_remote_count_v6 (family B sed present; flips
#     only when ESTAB v6 sockets are seeded post-boot — the F4 block
#     runs after the first audit). cannot-flip.
#   - security.suid_delta (family B sed present; flips only when a
#     "yesterday" .latest-counts.json is planted 10 below today's
#     suid count — the #38 mutated-count probe runs after the first
#     audit). cannot-flip.
#   - updates.security_delta (family B sed present; flips only when a
#     "yesterday" security_pending count is planted 10 below today's —
#     same #38 mutated-count probe). cannot-flip.
#
#   Every OTHER check_id in the registry flips under its single-line
#   sed in the driver's baseline (verified by a full driver run).
#
# The driver (test/mutation-coverage.sh, separate card) reads this
# file, applies each entry to a scratch tree, re-runs the seeded
# tier-2 suite, and records FLIPPED (caught — good) or SURVIVED
# (uncovered surface — signal) per entry.

security.fail2ban_banned	scripts/box-audit.sh	s|json_push alert security.fail2ban_banned security |json_push alert security.fail2ban_bannedX security |
security.fail2ban_jail	scripts/box-audit.sh	s|json_push alert security.fail2ban_jail security |json_push alert security.fail2ban_jailX security |
security.new_port	scripts/box-audit.sh	s|json_push warn security.new_port security |json_push warn security.new_portX security |
security.outbound_remote_count	scripts/box-audit.sh	s|json_push warn security.outbound_remote_count security |json_push warn security.outbound_remote_countX security |	cannot-flip: the driver's pristine baseline seeds no ESTAB v4 sockets (issue-#53's v4 block in install-seeded.sh runs after the first audit), so the finding is absent-in-baseline and a single sed cannot flip it
security.outbound_remote_count_v6	scripts/box-audit.sh	s|json_push warn security.outbound_remote_count_v6 security |json_push warn security.outbound_remote_count_v6X security |	cannot-flip: the driver's pristine baseline seeds no ESTAB v6 sockets (F4's v6 block in install-seeded.sh runs after the first audit), so the finding is absent-in-baseline and a single sed cannot flip it
security.suid_delta	scripts/box-audit.sh	s|json_push warn security.suid_delta security |json_push warn security.suid_deltaX security |	cannot-flip: the driver's baseline sidecar (written by install.sh's verify-gate audit) reflects the same box state, so suid_delta = today - yesterday = 0; install-seeded.sh's #38 mutated-count probe plants 'yesterday = today - 10' only after the first audit, so the finding is absent-in-baseline and a single sed cannot flip it
updates.security_delta	scripts/box-audit.sh	s|json_push warn updates.security_delta updates |json_push warn updates.security_deltaX updates |	cannot-flip: the driver's baseline sidecar (written by install.sh's verify-gate audit) reflects the same box state, so security_delta = today - yesterday = 0; install-seeded.sh's #38 mutated-count probe plants 'yesterday = today - 10' only after the first audit, so the finding is absent-in-baseline and a single sed cannot flip it
updates.security_pending	scripts/box-audit.sh	s|json_push warn updates.security_pending updates |json_push warn updates.security_pendingX updates |
system.failed_units	scripts/box-audit.sh	s|json_push warn system.failed_units system |json_push warn system.failed_unitsX system |
system.cron_d_dropins	test/install-docker/seeded/seed.sh	s|^printf .fake-cron-line|: # F6-registry mutation removes the cron.d drop-in (family A)|
security.ssh_fails	scripts/box-audit.sh	s|json_push warn security.ssh_fails security |json_push warn security.ssh_failsX security |
system.user_cron	scripts/box-audit.sh	s|json_push warn system.user_cron system |json_push warn system.user_cronX system |
maintenance.apt_cache_stale	scripts/box-audit.sh	s|json_push warn maintenance.apt_cache_stale maintenance "stale |json_push warn maintenance.apt_cache_staleX maintenance "stale |
integrity.change	scripts/box-audit.sh	s|integrity.change integrity|integrity.changeX integrity|g
